::MCR_U03_L05_Quiz_Q01::
Question ID: MCR_U03_L05_Quiz_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.DL.3
Question:
Which response best supports this correlation and causation skill: identify correlation without claiming causation?
{
=A. Use cautious claim language and connect the conclusion to the evidence.#Correct. Responsible data interpretation avoids claiming causation unless the evidence supports it.
~B. Claim that association always proves causation.#This is the common misconception; association alone does not prove cause and effect.
~C. Ignore other possible explanations.#Other factors can explain an observed relationship.
~D. Reject all data claims automatically.#Data claims should be evaluated carefully, not automatically rejected.
}


